<title>USA: FGIC qualifies 11 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies 11 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 11 municipal bond issues slated for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Connecticut $77.5 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Burke County, Fla., $2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Burke County, Fla., $18.765 million GO and refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Fayettevile, N.C., $16.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Stokes County, N.C., $8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Campbell-Savona Central School District, N.Y., $3.4 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Westhill Central School District, N.Y., $4.2 million GO school bonds.</p>
<p>--Pittsburgh, Pa., $167.44 million GO and refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Pottsgrove School District, Pa., $4.995 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Franklin County, Tenn., $14 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Texas $50 million taxable veterans bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
